      "body": "This publishes the ThreeCore read-only wallet and offline rehearsal development checkpoint. Resuming a previously permitted wallet no longer requires copying its public address into the form: a new explicit preview reads existing site permission, rechecks the same address and network before applying it, and leaves Connect as a separate action. The existing identity checks, protection stops and idle policy remain in force. Wallet/rehearsal links also open a separate tab to preserve the original page's unsaved work.\n\nRelease verification includes the bounded source-package verifier, evidence-integrity CI, reviewed restoration/cancellation and stale-result fixes, plus Japanese operator instructions. Report-review tests wait for asynchronous digest completion; the delayed-digest control fails before the fix and passes after it.\n\nValidation:\n- [Latest CI at 07041f0](https://github.com/FordPerfect2027/ThreeCore-Wallet/actions/runs/41311235726): all five jobs passed; 15,978 regression tests, 431 HTTP tests and three consecutive runs of 1,004 synthetic browser UI tests passed.\n- [Account reconnection report](https://github.com/FordPerfect2027/ThreeCore-Wallet/blob/07041f00efdb503cb76a06fbe12e5531cb380930/docs/ACCOUNT_RECONNECTION_2026-11-01.md): 116 focused cases and 1,004 synthetic browser UI cases passed locally. Coverage includes cancelled/delayed RPC, account/network changes, stopped access, reviewed input, duplicate-card rejection and explicit connection.\n- On the intended PC, existing MetaMask permission exposed the operator-selected account; the EMA card connected and read registered contract metadata/balance. Actual files and a named checkpoint were saved. After page reload, reviewed restore, Stop/Resume and explicit reconnect succeeded. Live account details and screenshots remain local; the public test logs contain synthetic data.\n- [Actual rehearsal recovery](https://github.com/FordPerfect2027/ThreeCore-Wallet/blob/b6989aa66dd6ae48b38ad963704deafb776987bd/docs/OPERATOR_RECOVERY_2026-11-01.md) preserved six fictional records and three cases across save, ordinary file selection, cancellation, confirmed restore and re-export. Both 17,387-byte exports match exactly and are published with checksums.\n- [Japanese operator guide](https://github.com/FordPerfect2027/ThreeCore-Wallet/blob/07041f00efdb503cb76a06fbe12e5531cb380930/docs/OPERATOR_ACCEPTANCE_JA.md) covers permitted-address preview, named resume checkpoints, preservation, backups, restoration and connection failures.\n- [Source-package checkpoint](https://github.com/FordPerfect2027/ThreeCore-Wallet/blob/f81c600918360daee77c1736915ac8878f02cb65/docs/SOURCE_CHECKPOINT_2026-11-01.md): 4,227 exported files matched the named earlier commit df9690f7d1b2c1d3a66e104e506a6ac8c732d86f; seven isolated startup checks and eight verifier regressions passed. This is an earlier package, not a package of the latest revision.\n- [Earlier 600-item checkpoint](https://github.com/FordPerfect2027/ThreeCore-Wallet/blob/f81c600918360daee77c1736915ac8878f02cb65/docs/CONTINUATION_600_COMPLETION_2026-11-01.md) retains its own evidence. [Current release gates](https://github.com/FordPerfect2027/ThreeCore-Wallet/blob/07041f00efdb503cb76a06fbe12e5531cb380930/docs/RELEASE_READINESS_2026-11-01.md) distinguish completed checks from the remaining public-testnet multi-account acceptance, full history recovery, independent review and release decision.\n\nThis remains a development draft. A single live Base Mainnet account is not three distinct public-testnet accounts. Address preview neither grants additional permission nor establishes ownership, and restoring settings does not restore a connection. Source publication and test counts do not establish a mainnet-readiness percentage. Signing, transfers, approval transactions and private-key retrieval remain outside scope.",
